'''Komori''' is an [[:Category:Uber Rare Cats|Uber Rare Cat]] that can be obtained from the [[Cat Capsule#Rare Capsule|Rare Capsule]] during the [[Nature's Guardians ELEMENTAL PIXIES (Gacha Event)|Nature's Guardians ELEMENTAL PIXIES]] gacha event. It was added in [[Version 14.6 Update|Version 14.6]].

{{Cat Info
|ID = 817
|rarity = UR
|name1 = Komori
|name2 = Moririn
}}

==Evolution==
Evolves into '''Moririn''' at level 10.

==Strategy/Usage==
Moririn has a deceptively broad niche at first glance, however struggles at putting any of its abilities to good use. [[Curse]] is just not useful on most [[:Category:Dark Enemies|Dark enemies]], since they seldom rely on abilities that are affected by Curse in the first place. Its matchups against [[:Category:Colossus Enemies|Colossus]] and [[:Category:Behemoth Enemies|Behemoth]] enemies are decent, as it can disable [[Casaurian Darkjo]]'s Toxic, [[Crocodylidae Kurocroc]]'s Weaken, and [[Super Hyppoh]]'s Slow, all while dealing good DPS. However, many of these enemies are often accompanied by more problematic supports that neglect its effective usage, not to mention the fact that their abilities are often not what makes them dangerous. This leaves [[:Category:Alien Enemies|Aliens]] as the most practical use case, where it can see a fair amount of potential usage in countering [[Nimoy Bore]], [[Elder Sloth]], or [[Mesocosmocyclone]], among others. Notably, Curse can disable [[Warp]], which can be very helpful in certain stages. That said, it still falls short when compared to the likes of [[Bakery Cat (Rare Cat)|Fried Chicken Cat]], which is more readily available and spammable.

On a fundamental level, Moririn's high knockback count prevents it from being a good tanker, despite its somewhat impressive effective HP. It has an incredibly low DPS usually, and the nature of Curse means the utility in its own niche varies on a case-by-case basis depending on whether an enemy's ability is the most dangerous part of their kit, which it often isn't. It is also not recommended for use in mixed stages, since its HP without [[Resistant]] does not allow it to tank any amount of damage at all. Its [[Conjure]] is quite useful, however, and serves to double its own effective HP for close to 7 seconds. Be sure to time it well to get the most value from it and Moririn. Its guaranteed [[Barrier Breaker]] also makes it quite useful for [[Cats of the Cosmos]], just like every other [[Nature's Guardians ELEMENTAL PIXIES (Gacha Event)|Elemental Pixie]].

